"Bye-laws" means any bye-laws made by the Board pursuant to
the powers conferred by the Act and the Rules;

"Category" means any category of membership of the Corporation
constituted under the Rules;

"Chairman" means the Chairman of the Corporation appointed by
section 13 of the Act, or the Chairman of the Corporation for the time
being-eleeted_by_the-Board-under Rule 81;

"Change Notice" means a notice to the Board given by a Member
pursuant to Rule 13 or Rule 14;

"Class" means any class of membership of the Corporation cons-
tituted under the Rules;

_ "Class Meeting" means a separate meeting of any Class, or a
joint meeting of any two or more Classes duly convened pursuant to
Rule 53;

"Class Representative' means a Director elected or appointed
under the Rules as a representative of a Class on the Board;

"Clearing House" means any Clearing House established pursuant
to the Act and the Rules and includes any joint Clearing House
established as aforesaid by the Corporation jointly with any trade
association ;

"Corporation" means any body corporate wherever established
registered or incorporated under the provisions of any written law,
Royal Charter or other instrument;

"The Corporation" means the Federation of Malaya Rubber
Exchange constituted under the Act;

"Dealer" means a Member who is registered as a member of the
Dealers Class constituted under the Rules;

"defaulter" means a Member so described in Rule 22 and a person
against whom action has been taken under Rule 23;

"Deputy Chairman" means the Deputy Chairman of the Corporation
appointed by section 13 of the Act or the Deputy Chairman of the
Corporation-for-the-time being elected by the Board under Rule 81;

"Director" means a member of the Board for the time being and
includes an Alternate Director whilst he is acting as such;

"Rstates' Selling Agent" means a Member who is registered as a
member of the Estates' Selling Agents Class constituted under the Rules;

"Extraordinary General Meeting" means a General Meeting con-
vened pursuant to Rule 29;

"First Members" means the persons whose names are set out in
the First Schedule to the Act;

"general meeting" means any meeting of the Corporation duly
convened pursuant to the Rules;

"Guarantee Broker" means any Broker who is authorised under the
Rules, bye-laws or regulations to enter into guarantee contracts;

"Guarantee Contract" means a contract in a form prescribed by
the Rules, bye-laws or regulations, and made by a Guarantee Broker
acting on behalf of a principal whose name is not disclosed, in terms
of which, and subject to such conditions as may be prescribed, the
Broker guarantees the performance of the contract by his principal;

"Guarantee Fund" means a fund established by the Board pursuant
to Rule 59 (c);

